    "question": "What is the main difference between SQL and NoSQL databases?",
    "answer": "Well, SQL databases are relational, so they use tables with fixed rows and columns to store data, which is good for structure. NoSQL databases, on the other hand, don't use tables. They use things like documents or key-value pairs instead. This makes NoSQL much more flexible when you have unstructured data, though it can be harder to query sometimes if you are used to traditional databases.",
