    "question": "What are the main differences between a delta and an estuary?",
    "answer": "I know they both happen where a river meets the ocean. A delta is where the river dumps a lot of sand and sediment, building up a triangular shape with different channels. On the other hand, an estuary is more of an open bay where the fresh river water mixes directly with the salty ocean water. So, one is more about sediment buildup, while the other is focused on the mixing of water types.",
